Everything works as specified. Summary of changes:

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added `filter_by_tag` after `ordered_pinned_first`:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact-match filter (`==` on each tag), preserves relative order, returns owned references.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — `list` now accepts `--tag <TAG>` (and `--tag=<TAG>`). When present, output is filtered through `filter_by_tag`; otherwise all notes print as before.

Verification:
- `cargo build` and `cargo test` pass (2 existing tests green).
- End-to-end CLI run confirms: `--tag rust` returns only notes with an exact `rust` tag (case-sensitive — `#Rust` excluded), `--tag <absent>` returns nothing, and no flag lists everything in original order.

One behavior worth flagging: matching is case-sensitive (so `rust` ≠ `Rust`), matching the exact-match contract. Let me know if you'd prefer case-insensitive matching.


